<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xinca people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xinca are an indigenous people of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, living mainly in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of Santa Rosa and neighbouring areas near the Pacific coast. Unlike most indigenous Guatemalans they are not Maya, and their language, Xinca, is unrelated to the Mayan languages. It is now nearly extinct, though the community has worked to revive it and is officially recognised alongside the Maya and Garífuna.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xinca-people.jpg" alt="Xinca people" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gobierno de Guatemala · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L%C3%ADderes_del_Parlamento_Xinca_en_Guatemala_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
